Here's the structured goal model for the multi-robot system delivering food and retrieving dishes in a hospital setting:

### Goals Table

| Goal ID | Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|---------|-------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1      | Deliver Food and Retrieve Dishes | Ensure food delivery and dish retrieval are completed successfully. | - | Achieve | - |
| G2      | Deliver Food to Patient Room | Deliver food to the patient's room. | (FALLBACK(G2.1, G2.2)) | Perform | AND (with G3) |
| G3      | Retrieve Dishes from Patient Room | Retrieve dirty dishes from the patient's room. | (FALLBACK(G3.1, G3.2)) | Achieve | AND (with G2) |
| G2.1    | Place Meal on Table | Deliver meal directly onto the room table. | - | Task | OR (with G2.2) |
| G2.2    | Place Meal on Tray | Deliver meal onto the robot's tray. | - | Task | OR (with G2.1) |
| G2.3    | Determine Patient Capability | Check if the patient can retrieve the meal. | - | Query | AND (with G2.1, G2.2) |
| G3.1    | Retrieve Dishes Unassisted | Retrieve dishes without assistance. | - | Task | OR (with G3.2) |
| G3.2    | Retrieve Dishes Assisted | Retrieve dishes with assistance. | - | Task | OR (with G3.1) |
| G4      | Open Room Door | Open the door to the patient's room. | (FALLBACK(G4.1, G4.2)) | Achieve | AND (with G2, G3) |
| G4.1    | Open Door Unassisted | Open door without assistance. | - | Task | OR (with G4.2) |
| G4.2    | Open Door Assisted | Open door with human assistance. | - | Task | OR (with G4.1) |
| G5      | Alert Wrong Meal Retrieved | Alert if the wrong meal is retrieved. | - | Perform | AND (with G2) |

### Tasks Table

| Task ID | Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots |
|---------|-------|------|----------|----------|-------------------|
| AT1     | Place Meal on Table | Deliver meal directly onto the room table. | OR (with AT2) | Patient's Room | 1 |
| AT2     | Place Meal on Tray | Deliver meal onto the robot's tray. | OR (with AT1) | Patient's Room | 1 |
| AT3     | Determine Patient Capability | Check if the patient can retrieve the meal. | AND (with G2.1, G2.2) | Hospital Database | 1 |
| AT4     | Retrieve Dishes Unassisted | Retrieve dishes without assistance. | OR (with AT5) | Patient's Room | 1 |
| AT5     | Retrieve Dishes Assisted | Retrieve dishes with assistance. | OR (with AT4) | Patient's Room | [1,2] |
| AT6     | Open Door Unassisted | Open door without assistance. | OR (with AT7) | Patient's Room | 1 |
| AT7     | Open Door Assisted | Open door with human assistance. | OR (with AT6) | Patient's Room | 1 |
| AT8     | Alert Wrong Meal Retrieved | Alert if the wrong meal is retrieved. | AND (with G2) | Patient's Room | 1 |

### Summary of Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3** [AND]
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2** [OR] with FALLBACK
- **G2 -> G2.3** [AND]
- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2** [OR] with FALLBACK
- **G4 -> G4.1, G4.2** [OR] with FALLBACK
- **G2.1 -> AT1** [AND]
- **G2.2 -> AT2** [AND]
- **G3.1 -> AT4** [AND]
- **G3.2 -> AT5** [AND]
- **G4.1 -> AT6** [AND]
- **G4.2 -> AT7** [AND]
- **G5 -> AT8** [AND]

This model ensures that the system can handle both food delivery and dish retrieval efficiently, considering various assistance scenarios and fallback options for robust operation.
